<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indira Kala Sangeet Vishwavidyalaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1956</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indira Kala Sangeet Vishwavidyalaya is a university of music, dance and fine arts at Khairagarh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in 1956. Raja Birendra Bahadur Singh and Rani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pawaya">Padmavati</a> of the former princely state of Khairagarh gave their palace for it and named it after their daughter Indira. It was one of the first universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> devoted to music and the performing arts.</p></div>
